## Now / next — Stage 4: the consumer-boundary eval unification (THE LINCHPIN)
**CORE SUBSTRATE COMPLETE + PROVEN (2026-06-09, tick 5).** All three boundaries eval
state-DATA → runnable, each backed by a GREEN consumer. The remaining Stage-4 work is the
SURFACE eval (lang 4a, now LIVE) + the recognition (unify 4b) + the `realize` retirement
(lang) — core has handed off and is **available to pair**, not blocked.
The thesis (`homoiconic-unification.md` Stage 4 + Constructor face): **one eval = eval
DATA → runnable at EVERY consumer boundary.** *This is what dissolves the FLAT/RICH constructor
seam* (lets reaction/pattern constructors produce DATA like process/composite):
- [x] **nodes** — SUBSTRATE DONE. `Core::instantiate_spec` (`core.rs:165`) reads the
      `{_type,address,config}` envelope → `ProcessNode` (the single-node surface entry); the
      engine's `discover_processes` (`engine.rs:1486`) evals a spec the same way. PROVEN
      end-to-end: `reaction_creates_process.rs` — a reactum `_add`s a process/composite SPEC and
      the engine evals it into a LIVE ticking node (process AND composite). 4a SURFACE is lang's
      and **LIVE** (lang tick 11, planned `metacircular_node_rung` test, building against core-green).
      Seam handed off: surface `eval` calls `instantiate_spec` (single node) or
      `Engine::from_state`+`discover_all_processes` (whole program). 4b (unify the `meta`
      `eval`/`load` with the engine rung) — I see NO real duplication (different rungs); unify to confirm/close.
- [x] **rules** — `collect_reactions`/`push_reaction` (`brs.rs`): DONE (4c). `push_reaction`
      now evals a TRANSPARENT reaction-DATA map (`_pat="Rule"`) via the existing
      `ReactionRule::from_data_value`, additive beside the `Foreign` carrier — symmetric with
      `discover_processes`. Consumer: `prism-bigraph/tests/reaction_data_as_state.rs` (3 green).
      lang's flip is DONE (every producer emits DATA; FLAT/RICH dissolved); `ReactionType::realize`
      retirement is lang's deferred cleanup (ripples to reaction_type + distributed_alchemy tests).
- [x] **patterns** — SUBSTRATE DONE. `Pattern::from_value` (`prism_schema::reaction`) is total +
      lawed (`reaction_data.rs`) and reused *inside* `from_data_value`, so 4c already carries it.
      A standalone `find_matches`-from-DATA entry (4d) is consumer-driven — only if lang's
      `count()`/`.matches()` want it.
- [x] **Unify the three as ONE "eval data→runnable" op/pattern** — DONE IN SPIRIT. The
      recognition lives in `schema-algebra.md` § "Eval: state-data → runnable" (the shared shape:
      *scan state for a typed value, eval to runnable, collect*), each boundary an EXISTING codec.
      A LITERAL single function would be a FALSE unification: 3 distinct runnable types
      (`ProcessNode`/`ReactionRule`/matcher) consumed by 3 distinct machineries
      (`engine.nodes`/BRS ruleset/`find_matches`) — it would just re-split. "Not a new operation,
      a shared shape" (the doc) is the correct closure.

## Coordinate
`prism-schema` + `prism-bigraph` are SHARED crates everyone builds on — a public-API or
BRS/reaction-boundary change is **NON-MONOTONE** → **coordinate-FIRST** (read `board.ys`,
claim it in `touching`, drop a `note` so lang/domains rebuild). The Stage-4 gate is **LIFTED**
(lang 2b green @ tick 10–11, simplify Stage-3 green @ tick 6). lang is **LIVE on 4a** (the
surface `eval` / `metacircular_node_rung`), building against core's published GREEN
(schema+bigraph @ green_tick 5). Core's role now: **pair the seam** (substrate is ready, no
edits needed) + be the green watermark lang/simplify build on. **Do NOT** start the next
non-monotone core arc (#71 units-in-schema — a `Schema`-enum change) in-tree mid-push; it
would break lang's 4a build. It lands as ONE coordinated/isolated arc at the post-push green
checkpoint. Pair with `unify` on the recognition, `lang` on the chrysalis↔prism seam.

